WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.300
- [Narrator:] There's a singular moment,

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.970
something most people will never realize,

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.210
where all your efforts
culminate to deliver your dream,

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.310
where you realize your purpose.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.660
For Cole Anthony, that was now,

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.130
back home in NYC and
ready for the NBA draft.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.587
But it wasn't that simple.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.550
[A collage of different news reporters' voices begins]
- In just this hour...

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.840
- Chinese authorities have
traced a new deadly virus back

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.120
to the city of Wuhan.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.570
- The symptoms include fever,
difficulty breathing.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.640
- The first coronavirus
death confirmed in the U.S.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.470
- The number of coronavirus cases jumped

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.600
by nearly 5,000 here in the United States.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.510
- This has been quick,
fierce, fast and ferocious.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.503
- We have never seen
anything like this before.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:52.288
- [Cole Anthony:] I was never expecting
it to get to this level.

00:00:52.288 --> 00:00:54.130
I thought they would have
had it under control by now.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:57.350
But it's really just gotten
out of hand, which is crazy.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.183
- [Donald Trump:] I'm officially

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.470
declaring a national emergency.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.770
[A collage of different news reporters' voices begins]
- The coronavirus crisis

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.570
is changing so fast.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.160
The great shutdown of 2020 is underway.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.110
- More than three-quarters of Americans

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:11.180
are under stay-at-home orders tonight.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.210
- [Cole Anthony:] Just being in New York,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.060
being at the center of all this madness,

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.420
I've seen that it's a lot of
people suffering right now.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.930
I haven't really had
that experience in New York,

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.733
cuz they have everything shut down.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.920
- [Casey Stern:] There are probably a lot of things that,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.740
and as a dad, G.A., with your experience,

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:35.170
you think about basketball and his life,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:38.050
no one's ever been through
what we're all going through.

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:40.270
What have conversations been
like between the two of you?

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.760
- Just me and my dad have
been pretty much talking

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.370
once every couple days.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.203
You know, there's been a few times

00:01:45.203 --> 00:01:46.730
where he hadn't reached
out to me for a while
[Greg Anthony laughing]

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.517
and I had to pretty
much reach my hand out

00:01:49.517 --> 00:01:51.230
and try to make sure he was still alive.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.920
Just the fact that this is something

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.120
that a lot of people
can go several lifetimes

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.210
without ever enduring,

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.810
it's really crazy.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.160
[A collage of different news reporters' voices begins]
- The entire sports world

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.450
just come to a complete halt.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.130
- It must be crushing to
some of the players.

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.460
- Reports are that the NBA likely

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:06.440
will be pushing back the
start date of the NBA draft.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.430
- [Cole Anthony:] Due to corona,

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.450
I don't really think it's changed my path.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.570
I don't think it's changed much

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.160
just in terms of my basketball.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.700
I think it's just really
given me the opportunity

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.600
to just be laser-focused,
just to really focus on what matters

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.900
at this point in my life,
which is basketball.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.590
- [Trainer:] Nice. Good work.

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.270
One, two, switch those feet, pull up.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.620
Way to shoot. Way to shoot.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.230
- A normal day in New York...

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.600
I got into a pretty
comfortable routine.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:36.720
They closed the gym that I go to,

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.080
but they're letting us
get special access after hours.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.280
I mean, I've pretty much changed my whole schedule

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.990
just so that I can get in the gym at night.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.340
And then rest and repeat.
Same thing, every day.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.173
- [Trainer:] Stay with it.

00:02:47.173 --> 00:02:48.080
You're all right. Let's go.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.200
Get downhill. Get
downhill. Get to the rim.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.910
- [Cole Anthony:] I've been really in
there with these workouts.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:55.200
And whenever I get into the
gym, I go super hard.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.940
Going 120 percent whenever I get in.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.670
So I don't think I'm
gonna fall off too hard

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.420
just from getting out of game-shape.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.090
- [Trainer:] Kick, kick.
Let's go. Get up. Get up.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.350
- To me, I think a lot of people

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:06.600
are gonna use this as an excuse

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.890
to pretty much stop playing basketball,

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.300
just stop working, stop working hard.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.490
And I just, I don't look for excuses.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:15.690
I look for just every advantage I can get.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.225
Try to stay ahead of the pack.

00:03:17.225 --> 00:03:19.475
- [Trainer:] Put it down hard.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.450
- [Narrator:] With nothing
to do and nowhere to go,

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.710
Cole only had one mindset: grind.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:29.010
Despite everything going on in the world,

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.560
Cole took this chance to
get out of the spotlight

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.150
and just work.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.610
- [Jonathan Wasserman:] I don't think the coronavirus is going

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.670
to affect Cole Anthony's draft stock.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.270
People are gonna forget
that North Carolina

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:39.880
wasn't gonna make the NCAA tournament

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.090
because nobody's gonna know

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.550
who was actually supposed to
get to the NCAA tournament.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:44.383
- [Franklyn Calle:] I think, in general,

00:03:44.383 --> 00:03:46.420
it's been a very weird
college basketball season, right?

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:49.710
You had a lot of the top
players who weren't even playing.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.239
LaMelo Ball wasn't playing in college.

00:03:51.239 --> 00:03:53.750
RJ Hampton wasn't playing in college.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.370
James Wiseman barely played in college.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.270
Cole Anthony was battling injuries.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:03:59.540
So a lot of the big names

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.750
weren't really even
playing college basketball.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.130
I'm very curious, if you're an NBA scout,

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.690
based on whatever happened this season,

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:07.540
how do you even evaluate all of this?

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:12.170
[A collage of different analysts' voices begins]
- Cole Anthony came in with as much hype

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:14.610
as you could possibly
come in with to college.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.840
- He was, I think, NBA-ready

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.200
when he was a junior in high school.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.110
- Perplexing freshman
season to say the least.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:22.680
-  Whenever you have a
really explosive player

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.700
and they have a knee injury,

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.930
it does take a hit on their draft stock.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.880
- I would be able to overlook

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.210
that North Carolina season.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.250
- Cole is someone who, at every stage,

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.490
has been able to go through
some bumps and bruises

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.663
and then excel.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:41.290
- He came in with a lot
of hype, Cole Anthony did.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:43.020
Unfortunately with the knee injury,

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.100
his season was cut short.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.010
- His whole year was incomplete
because he had the injury.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.010
Then he had a team that really struggled.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.990
He wasn't able to really
fulfill those expectations.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.250
- He was gonna be a top-10 pick

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.970
regardless. The pieces around
him just weren't good enough

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:58.440
to show how good of a point guard

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.770
I believe this young man could truly be.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.840
- I think a lot of, like, kids
just have not dealt

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.182
with adversity to this level.

00:05:04.182 --> 00:05:05.710
A lot of kids are just
used to it going their way,

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.640
used to winning the
majority of their games.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.220
Really haven't dealt with losing seasons,

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:10.800
haven't dealt with just the struggles,

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.430
the hardships of a season like that.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:14.980
So I think all it could do
is benefit me in the future.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.330
- Big picture with Cole Anthony,

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.430
I mean, he still averaged 20
points a game this year,

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.240
and 6'3", athletic.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:23.400
And again, you're projecting
long-term potential.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.710
I don't think teams put too
much stock into what happens

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:29.693
during a 20-, 30-game
sample size in college.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.870
- [Narrator:] The uncertainty
had been crushing.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.360
Draft on hold. Quarantine.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.530
Midnight workouts. 
No clarity on the future.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:44.110
And finally it was announced:

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.483
NBA draft was slated for November 18th.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.820
Next step in Cole's journey has arrived.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.910
- [Cole Anthony:] I just think that, to whatever team

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:52.900
wants to take a chance on me,

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.310
I just think you'll get
someone who's gonna work

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:58.030
as hard as they can every single day,

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:01.910
not gonna make excuses,
just gonna get in there, work,

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.360
try to make everyone around them better.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.510
I promise they will
not regret drafting me.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.730
- [Interviewer:] There's
rumors that, you know, the Knicks

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:09.750
might be involved.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.160
Would you like to go to the
Knicks cuz of New York?

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.160
- I mean, look, hey, it would be cool.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.990
I mean, I'd be blessed up to be
drafted to any team, though.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.580
So whatever team that is, I'm just,

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.680
I'll be very thankful
and grateful to them,

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.008
and I'll give them everything I can.

00:06:21.008 --> 00:06:22.050
- Knick posters!

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:23.290
- [Wassman:] I think Cole Anthony to the Knicks

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.580
would kind of bring back
some of that '90s love

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.403
that everybody had for the Knicks.
- [Announcer on footage:] Ewing! Oh, ho! Wow!

00:06:29.999 --> 00:06:31.290
- [Calle:] I think the city would get behind him

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.123
because he's one of us.

00:06:32.123 --> 00:06:34.570
He's a New York product.
Because he grew up here.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:36.620
He's absolutely not afraid of the life.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.340
- [Wasserman:] You want a guy who really wants to win

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:43.220
and is the type of guy who
can put a team on his back.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.290
And that's Cole Anthony.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.140
And he loves the moment.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.090
He loves the bright lights.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.990
I think that's...he's perfectly
suited for New York.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.740
- I truly haven't thought
about just having a legacy

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:51.573
just in New York.

00:06:51.573 --> 00:06:53.000
I just, I've thought bigger than that.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.120
I don't want to just be having
that legacy in New York.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:55.953
I wanna have a legacy

00:06:55.953 --> 00:06:57.730
that goes throughout the world.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:02.730
In the NBA, there are
those perennial All-Stars.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.630
There are those dudes who
are at the top of the league.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:10.030
And I just, I see myself
in that elite category.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.060
I mean, people might knock me for that.

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:12.997
That's where I see myself,

00:07:12.997 --> 00:07:15.123
and I'm going to hold
myself to that level.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.540
- [Narrator:] Cole came up a prodigal son

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.390
in New York's crowded basketball scene.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.253
Whether you believe he's
the next great point guard

00:07:23.253 --> 00:07:25.030
from the big city or not,

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:27.313
nobody can deny this kid's hunger.

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:29.620
♪♪♪ Gave my life to the game ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Had my mama concerned ♪♪♪

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:32.180
♪♪♪ It made her calm when she saw ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ What I got in return ♪♪♪

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.000
- [Narrator:] Dude wants to be a legend,

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.826
not in the shadow of his
pops, but in his own right.

00:07:37.826 --> 00:07:42.826
♪♪♪ Said I'mma be a legend soon ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ I'm a legend now ♪♪♪

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:46.520
- [Greg Anthony:] I was a stereotypical kid from the hood.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.510
And the game was gonna be my way

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.410
to do things in life that ordinarily

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.900
wouldn't be accomplished by people

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.890
that grew up like me, living where I lived,

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:01.144
which is completely different for my son.

00:08:01.144 --> 00:08:03.830
♪♪♪ I'm like Ali, I fight better ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ With my back on the ropes ♪♪♪

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.300
- [Calle:] He is as intense as he is

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.900
not because of some necessity reason.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.660
This dude really wants to
be really good at his craft.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:11.727
Money isn't driving it, you know,

00:08:11.727 --> 00:08:13.993
and I think that's the scary part of this.
♪♪♪ Checks overgrown ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Neck boulder stones ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Ever since they said I'm going pro ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ They said I'm the next so-and-so ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ But you know how it go ♪♪♪

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:24.520
- [Roy Williams:] My favorite part of
Cole's game is very easily

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.740
is he loves to play basketball.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:30.930
When I say loves, I mean
with a capital L-O-V-E-S,

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:33.240
all of them capitalized, bold print.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.710
Basketball is his deal.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.501
It's the real deal with him.

00:08:36.501 --> 00:08:38.945
♪♪♪ Broke my flow down ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ They still can't describe it in words ♪♪♪

00:08:38.945 --> 00:08:40.403
♪♪♪ And all the work they say they put in ♪♪♪

00:08:40.403 --> 00:08:41.760
♪♪♪ I gotta confirm ♪♪♪

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.540
- [Greg Anthony:] He's got a purity and a passion

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.710
just for the love of the game.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:50.650
The truly greats in our game
have always loved the game.

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:53.070
They don't fall in love with the life.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:56.053
They fall in love and
stay in love with the game.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:57.963
- I don't want to just make it

00:08:57.963 --> 00:08:59.653
to the NBA just to say I made it.
♪♪♪ Just so happens had a hunger for greatness, and I fed it ♪♪♪

00:09:02.578 --> 00:09:03.411
That's one thing that my dad tells me,

00:09:03.411 --> 00:09:04.500
that he had that regret.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.770
He didn't want to be great.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:06.930
My ultimate goal at basketball is

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:08.780
to be one of the best that ever played.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:12.776
♪♪♪ Said I'mma be a legend soon ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ I'm a legend now ♪♪♪

00:09:12.776 --> 00:09:15.438
♪♪♪ I'm a legend now ♪♪♪

00:09:15.438 --> 00:09:17.711
♪♪♪ They tried to tell me ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ I'mma be a legend soon, though ♪♪♪

00:09:17.711 --> 00:09:22.544
♪♪♪ But I'm a legend now ♪♪♪

